}

{
  "name": "Answering counterparty auditors' MTM valuation requests",
  "today": "Counterparties must show their auditors a third-party value of their trades with Enron, and ask Enron's Confirmations group (Larry Joe Hunter, Ellen Wallumrod) for it. Confirmations has no system that values deals, so it emails each request to all the gas desk heads (Gossett, Keiser, Love, Giron, Baumbach, McLaughlin). Each desk head forwards it to someone on the desk (Giron sends his to Patrick Ryder or Carole Frank), who runs a mini-book for that counterparty as of the requested date, blacks out the Delta/Vol columns, exports it to Excel and emails it back. Confirmations then has to collect the answers from each region. The requests seen in the mail all ask for the year-end close dates (Dec 29 and Dec 31, 2000).",
  "change": "Produce a month-end file of each counterparty's official MTM by region, so Confirmations can answer period-end audit requests itself without asking the desks.",
  "explanation": "At each month-end, a scheduled job takes the official (officialized) month-end books and writes the total MTM for each counterparty short name, by region, without Delta/Vol, to a file Confirmations can open. When an auditor asks for a counterparty's value as of a month-end or year-end date, a Confirmations clerk looks the counterparty up and sends the figure. Desk heads and book admins no longer receive, forward, run, black out and export mini-books for these requests. Requests for other dates still go to a desk until the EnTelligence system Hunter is planning, with back-dated curves, is built.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/240.eml",
      "quote": "Please forward to Ellen Wallumrod the MTM valuation(mini-book) for all \nCoEnergy Trading Company deals as of Dec 31, 2000.  If you can export into \nexcel and forward by e-mail, that would be appreciated."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/214.eml",
      "quote": "Can you provide MTM values as of Dec 29, 2000, for the short name of CROSS \nTIMBERS."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Two more counterparties need MTM values for Dec. 29, 2000."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "we'll need to continue to go to the different desks to provide Mark-to-Market \nvaluations for a Counterparty's portfolio.",
      "note": "Each request has to go out to several desks, and Confirmations then collects the answers from each."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "We do not have access to \nany system that values these deals, but are looking to get the on-line \n\"EnTelligence\" built so that it carries back-dated curves that will allow us \nto complete these requests without taking up a Risk person's time and without \nhaving to black out information (Delta/Vol) that is included in a mini-book.",
      "note": "The risk staff's time and the blacking out of Delta/Vol are the steps the change removes. Confirmations itself names them as the cost."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the total MTM value for that date within your region.",
      "note": "Each region answers separately, so one request becomes several pieces of work plus a step to combine them."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "Call Pat Ryder for West desk requests.",
      "note": "The desk head passes each request on to a book admin, which adds another person and another hand-off."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 3,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
    "quote": "we recieve several \nper week"
  },
  "minutes": 75
}

