{
  "name": "Monthly gas curve validation questions",
  "today": "Each month Jennifer Nguyen (curve validation) reviews 10 gas forward curves and emails questions about the ones that moved. In January she sent them to Jeff Gossett, who forwarded them to three desk heads (Giron, Love, Keiser); in February she sent them to all three desk heads, hoping the curves were 'covered between the three of you', and had to chase eight days later; in March she sent them to Darron Giron. The desk head then asks the trader and retypes the answer. When the answer is judged too thin (March), a second round goes back through the desk head to the trader, who repeats himself. Time is lost on several people reading questions that are not theirs, on the relay, the chaser and the second round.",
  "change": "Send each month's curve questions straight to the trader who owns each curve, cc the desk head, and say up front what kind of explanation is needed.",
  "explanation": "Curve validation keeps a short list of which trader and desk head own each gas curve (taken from existing curve ownership) and sends each flagged curve's question straight to its owner, cc the desk head, instead of to Gossett or all three desk heads. The question says what counts as an answer (the specific market events behind the move, not only 'the market traded higher'), and notes when a curve is set equal to another one (for example NGI-PGE Topock equals NGI-SOCAL) so it only gets asked once. Afterwards the trader answers once, the desk head sees it in copy, and Jennifer gets one answer per curve without relays, chasers or a second round.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/170.eml",
      "quote": "Attached are Powerpoint slides containg the \n10 curves that were validated for January."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/133.eml",
      "quote": "Attached are \nthe 10 curves reviewed for the month of February."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/49.eml",
      "quote": "Attached are Powerpoint slides containg the \n10 curves that were validated for March."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/170.eml",
      "quote": "Please get responses for these back to Jennifer today.",
      "note": "In January the questions went to Gossett, who passed them on to three desk heads; a manager step that direct routing removes."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/170.eml",
      "quote": "Phillip Allen and Keith Holst indicated that the curve changes in question \nfor Socal was simply due to a higher forward market.",
      "note": "The desk head is relaying what the traders said; the answer comes from the traders."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/133.eml",
      "quote": "Hopefully these curves are covered between the three of you!",
      "note": "Validation does not know which desk head owns each curve, so three people get every question."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/132.eml",
      "quote": "Can you or anyone in your group follow up on the curves below?",
      "note": "A chaser sent eight days after the February questions (13 Mar to 21 Mar), because nobody had picked them up."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/132.eml",
      "quote": "NGI-PGE/TOPOCK is an internal curve used to value transport and is equal to \nNGI-SOCAL.  This curve will probably show up every month",
      "note": "Some curves are set equal to another curve and will be asked about again each month; marking them saves a repeat question."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/47.eml",
      "quote": "However, we are \nlooking for specific reasons as to why this is so.",
      "note": "A second round in March because the first answer did not say what validation needed; saying so up front avoids it."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/47.eml",
      "quote": "I asked Keith Holst (trader) again.  His answer was the same.",
      "note": "The second round runs through the desk head to the trader and back."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": null,
  "minutes": 20
}

