{
  "name": "Monthly HPL Assignment, Termination & Expiration Report",
  "today": "Each month before bid week, Cheryl Dudley in Houston Pipe Line contract administration puts together a report of every contract assignment, termination and expiration her group has entered since the last report, whatever the effective date. She attaches it and emails it to a list of about 34 to 40 people. She also keeps the list herself: people email or phone her to be added or removed. Because the report depends on her remembering to do it, one month was missed: she did the February revision late and forgot the March report, so it went out on 8 March and the April report followed on 23 March.",
  "change": "Have the contract system produce the report on a fixed date before each bid week and email it to a list people join or leave themselves, so Cheryl only checks it.",
  "explanation": "A saved query in the contract system would pick out every assignment, termination and expiration entered since the last run, the same cut-off by entry date she uses today. It would lay the entries out in the report format and send them on a set date before bid week to a mail group that readers join or leave themselves. Cheryl would look over the output and fix anything odd. The report could no longer be skipped, and add or remove requests would not go through her. Readers would get the same report as before.",
  "occurrences": [
    {"file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/2114.eml", "quote": "Attached is a report \nfor March 2001 which covers all assignments, terminations & expirations \nentered since the last report was done on 2/15/01."},
    {"file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/2133.eml", "quote": "Attached is the April 2001 Assignment, Termination & Expiration Report for \nHouston Pipe Line's contracts."}
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {"file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/2114.eml", "quote": "Since I did the revision to the February 2001 report so late last month, I \naccidentally failed to do the report for March 2001.", "note": "Cheryl does the report herself on her own schedule, and a month was missed. A scheduled run would not skip a month."},
    {"file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/2114.eml", "quote": "There will be a new \nreport done around March 22nd in preparation for Bid Week.", "note": "The report is redone each month ahead of bid week, so it is regular monthly work."},
    {"file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/2133.eml", "quote": "It contains all of the entries made by \nour group since the report was last done on 3/8/01, regardless of the \neffective date.", "note": "The selection rule is simple and fixed (entries since the last run), so a saved query could apply it."},
    {"file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/2133.eml", "quote": "please let me know by e-mail or phone \n(x-36982) so that I can either remove your name from or add their name to the \ndistribution list.", "note": "Cheryl keeps the distribution list by hand. A list people manage themselves would take this off her."}
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": null,
  "minutes": 40
}

