{
  "name": "Transwestern shippers' short-term contract change requests",
  "change": "Shippers send MDQ increases and month-to-month continuations through a structured request; the account director approves with one click and the system produces the amendment for contract admin to check.",
  "reason": "The rate of 8-9 a month comes from a three-week burst (10 Dec 2001 - 3 Jan 2002): Lokay's sent mail runs from 29 Oct 2001 to 25 Mar 2002 and holds only about 10 such requests in all, about 2 a month, so at the proposal's own 15 minutes the saving is roughly 30 minutes a month, too little to pay for a shipper web form; the 15-minute amendment step is also assumed, and the same work was already rejected for this reason (decisions.md Rejected item 83).",
