{
  "name": "Chasing origination recognized on a book's P&L that does not match what was granted",
  "today": "When a trading book grants origination to an originator group (for example FT-Central to IM-Central / Middle Market), the grant goes on the origination schedule and the receiving book records the origination on its own P&L as a separate step. Each evening an analyst in the P&L group (Gabriel Monroy, Binh Pham, Rahmaan Mwongozi) compares what each book recognized with the schedule. When they differ, the analyst emails the desk head (Darron Giron) with Michael Benien and Chris Abel copied. The desk head then has to find out where the amount came from, either by asking the analyst or by forwarding to a book administrator (Scott Palmer, Kam Keiser) or another lead (Kevin Radous). The analyst chases items that are still open the next night. The work stalls because neither side can see the other's entry: the receiving book records amounts that were never granted, or does not record ones that were, and someone has to search across books to find who granted what.",
  "change": "Enter each origination grant once and have it post to both the granting book and the receiving book, so the receiving P&L cannot drift from the schedule.",
  "explanation": "The origination schedule becomes the only place a grant is entered (granting book, receiving origination group, deal, amount). That one entry posts the origination to the receiving book's P&L, so the book administrators stop keying it a second time. The analysts' nightly comparison then only has to catch the rare manual adjustment, and if one does turn up it goes straight to the book administrator named on the grant. Desk heads no longer relay these notices or search for who granted an amount.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/765.eml",
      "quote": "IM CENTRAL failed to recognize 468 (dollars) of the 9,488 that were granted \nto them by FT-Central on 06/15"
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/763.eml",
      "quote": "Darron, you recognized 3.975 (thousand) of orig, and I did not see that \ncoming out of any book. Could you let me know who granted that."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/722.eml",
      "quote": "There is still a remaining difference of  771.00 dollars that IM Central  \nand/ or  Chicago have not recognized on their P&L."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/695.eml",
      "quote": "Intracentral recognized $11,812 origination on their P&L that was not granted \non the origination schedule."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/677.eml",
      "quote": "Central origination claimed $750 more than what was granted to them."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/765.eml",
      "quote": "We recognized a total of $9,488 of Orig last night.  All from FT-Central.  Is \nthe $468 from another book?",
      "note": "The desk head cannot see where the difference comes from and has to ask back. Recognition is checked each night."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/763.eml",
      "quote": "Also, if you could please look into the 468 (dollars) that I \nmentioned on my previous email, I would appreciate it.",
      "note": "The analyst chases an item that is still open the next night. Giron forwarded this to Scott Palmer to research."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/722.eml",
      "quote": "Orig. Recognized on P&L \nIM - Central     54,252.00\nIM-Chicago    11,376.00\nTOTAL            65,628.00",
      "note": "The analyst builds the comparison of P&L totals against the schedule by hand. Five people are copied, and Giron forwards it on to Kevin Radous ('Have you heard about this?')."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/695.eml",
      "quote": "Could you please follow up on this.  Thanks.",
      "note": "The desk head relays the notice to two book administrators to research and fix."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/675.eml",
      "quote": "Did you grant the $750 in orig from the ticket I gave you yesterday?",
      "note": "The receiving side had recognized $750 before the grant was entered. It took four messages over two days to close, because the grant and the recognition are separate entries made by different people."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/675.eml",
      "quote": "I did not see this origination amount from Luchas.",
      "note": "The difference was still open the next night."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": null,
  "minutes": 40
}

